    "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. For q-133774, solving 2=-0.5x+9 gives x=14. For q-133965, the slope is -2 and the intercept is 90, so y(36)=18. For q-133943, the line is y=0.75x+0.25, giving x=9 when y=7. For q-117602, sine vanishes when 3x-π/4=nπ. For q-29132, cosine vanishes when x+45°=90°+180°n. For q-81532, sine is maximal when 4x+π/4=π/2+2nπ. For q-236971, using the degree convention established by the choices and solution, maxima occur when 3x=90°+360°n; this is equivalent to x=π/6+2nπ/3 in radians. For q-81536, cosine is minimal when x/3-π/4=π+2nπ. For q-117609, sine is minimal when 5x+π/2=-π/2+2nπ. For q-216042, clearing fractions and adding gives -6p=-18, then q=10. For q-75862, the cleared equations are 6x-y=6 and 2x-y=4, giving x=1/2 and y=-3. For q-52202, the cleared equations give -8w=40, then v=-3. For q-26094, substitution gives -14x-42=0, then y=3. For q-38546, both one-sided limits at -1 equal -1 while f(-1)=1, so all three statements are false. For q-73105, the left limit is 3 while the right limit and f(3) equal 1, so only statement II is true. For q-66027, the secant period is 2π/|1/3|=6π. Each MA answer below is supported by a verbatim quotation from that question's own captured solution; no submitted grade was supplied.",
